#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Runs the CI's two Windows jobs on a real Windows, in a VirtualBox virtual machine of this computer, over SSH, so that what fails on GitHub's windows-2025 fails here first.

  scripts/check-windows                       sync, lock, ruff, pytest and smoke in this order, each with its result line; a failed step stops none but sync
  scripts/check-windows --only NAME           only the steps named (repeatable): sync lock ruff pytest smoke (ruff and pytest need the environment that sync makes, so sync runs with them)
  scripts/check-windows -- ARGS...            ARGS go to pytest (`-- tests/test_replay.py -x`), which then is the one step that runs unless --only says more
  scripts/check-windows --snapshot NAME       puts the machine back to its snapshot NAME before it starts (only a machine that is powered off), for a clean Windows at every run
  scripts/check-windows --tty                 runs the pytest step in a session with a console (below) without trying a plain one first
  scripts/check-windows --install SETUP --snapshot NAME
                                              the install proof of a Windows trim instead: the machine put back to its clean snapshot, the installer (NeoAPRS-Setup-VERSION.exe) run silently, then the app's
                                              pieces and the uninstall, each a step (below)
  scripts/check-windows --upgrade OLD NEW --snapshot NAME
                                              the upgrade proof instead: the installer of the release before (OLD), a station made with it, then NEW installed over it as an update is (below)

Where the machine is comes from the environment, and nothing is guessed (CONVENTIONS.md has the table):
  NEOAPRS_WINVM              the VirtualBox name of the machine; unset means that the Windows check is not set up here, and the script says so and ends with 2
  NEOAPRS_WINVM_SSH_PORT     the port on this computer that is forwarded to the machine's SSH (it is reached at 127.0.0.1)
  NEOAPRS_WINVM_SSH_KEY      the private key it logs in with (a path: the script passes it to ssh and never reads it)
  NEOAPRS_WINVM_KNOWN_HOSTS  the known_hosts file that holds the machine's host key (a login with an unknown key fails: nothing is accepted on first use)
  NEOAPRS_WINVM_USER         the user on the machine, default John; its profile folder is C:\\Users\\USER
It is never a stage of scripts/check: it needs a machine that only some developers have, and minutes.

The machine. Powered off, it is started without a window (`VBoxManage startvm NAME --type headless`), the script waits for its SSH to answer and until the machine has been up for two minutes (Windows restarts its SSH service once in its first minute), and when the run is over the machine is shut down by
Windows's own shutdown, asked from inside over SSH and, when that has not turned it off, by the ACPI power button, and waited for; never a hard power-off, and if it does not go off in time it is left as it is and the script says so. A machine that was running
is left running. One run at a time: a lock file in the build cache ($NEOAPRS_BUILD_CACHE, default ~/.cache/neoaprs-build), one for each machine; a second run says so and stops.

The tree goes over as it is on disk, packed by scripts/check-in-container (its functions are loaded from that file: one reading of git's list, one place that keeps what an ignore rule names and every
file of access tokens, `.secrets` and what follows, on this computer). The tar is copied with scp and unpacked by Windows's own tar.exe into C:\\Users\\USER\\neoaprs-check\\RUN-<UTC time>\\neoaprs; the folders
of older runs are removed but the newest two. Where the machine has git, the tree there is a repository of one commit made of the tracked files, as the container does it (the tests ask git which files
are tracked); where it has none, those tests fail on it, as they do on a runner without git. uv lives in C:\\Users\\USER\\neotest\\uv: when that is not the pinned version (UV below, with its SHA-256, as
scripts/security-tools pins a program) the zip is fetched once into the build cache, checked and copied over. The Python that uv needs it fetches itself (UV_PYTHON_PREFERENCE=only-managed), of the version the workflow names (UV_PYTHON).

The steps are the CI's commands in the order of ci.yml, as the job `python` runs them on Windows (UV_FROZEN=1, which the lock step takes away as the workflow's `env -u` does) and the job `smoke` (the
wheel built, a fresh environment, the wheel installed there, scripts/smoke.py with the installed command), written in PowerShell. Every step runs with NEOAPRS_NO_DEVICES=1, NEOAPRS_UPDATE_CHECK=0 and
UV_PYTHON_PREFERENCE=only-managed. A line for each step as scripts/check prints it (`ok` or `FAIL`, the name, the seconds); under a failed step the end of its output, and the whole log of every step
is kept in the folder that the first line names, on this computer. Commands go to the machine as one PowerShell script in `-EncodedCommand` form, so that no name or path is read by two shells.

A test that is run over SSH has no console of its own, and some tests need one: a child that a test started in its own process group (tests/support/proc.py: CREATE_NEW_PROCESS_GROUP, used by the
daemon tests, the replay commands of tests/test_scripts.py and tests/test_replay.py, and scripts/smoke.py) is ended with Ctrl+Break, which Windows delivers only inside a console that the sender is
attached to. Before the pytest step the script runs a probe of that in the same kind of session (a child in a new process group, Ctrl+Break sent, it must end). A plain `ssh HOST COMMAND` is tried first:
sshd starts the command with a hidden console, which should be enough. If the probe fails there, the step runs through `ssh -tt`, which gives it a pseudo console (ConPTY), and the output is cleaned of
its escape sequences. Tried on the machine (13 November 2026): the probe passes in the plain session; the power button alone did not shut a Windows down that nobody was looking at, which is
why the shutdown is asked from inside first. Not tried: whether `ssh -tt` with its input held open ends cleanly at the command's end; --tty skips the plain try.

The install proof (--install) is the scripted part of the clean install that every Windows trim of what is shipped must pass (docs/development.md, "On a real Windows"). Its steps: install (silent:
/VERYSILENT /SUPPRESSMSGBOXES /NORESTART; the files, the Start menu, the installed size), defender (real-time protection must be on; the scan of the folder, MpCmdRun, only where the account is an
administrator, never through a UAC prompt), daemon (Stop NeoAPRS with nothing running, `neoaprsw.exe run` on the default data folder, the page and the world map it ships, its name in Task Manager,
Stop NeoAPRS again), commands (`neoaprs.exe --version`, `doctor`, `support`), app (`neoaprs-app.exe --tray` starts its daemon, its name in Task Manager, `neoaprs.exe stop` ends both), map (a map cut,
a dry run), direwolf (the installed app finds its own Direwolf: `neoaprs.exe db radios add direwolf` on a fresh folder, and the installed direwolf.exe runs as the pinned release),
smoke (scripts/smoke.py against the installed neoaprs.exe), mercury (packaging/windows/smoke_mercury.py on the installed mercury.exe) and uninstall (with the app running: the program
folder gone, nothing left in it, the start at sign-in and the processes gone, the data folder kept). The steps before smoke run on a machine with nothing but Windows and the app; uv and its Python come
only then. Nothing follows a failed install.

The upgrade proof (--upgrade OLD NEW) is the one test, before a release is public, that a station of the release before comes through the update on Windows. Its steps, each needing the one before (the first that
fails ends it; the machine is shut down all the same): old (OLD installed silently as above, its files, `neoaprs.exe --version` the version of its file name), station (with that release's own command line only:
`neoaprs.exe db --data FOLDER set KEY VALUE` for the flat keys of STATION, the Dummy radio as the FM radio and the Dummy HF radio as the HF one, so that no device is needed; then its daemon `neoaprsw.exe run --data
FOLDER --web-port 0` for RUN_SEC with NEOAPRS_UPDATE_CHECK=0, its page, `neoaprs.exe stop --data FOLDER`; then its `db list` and `db stations`, printed and kept in files of the run's folder), update (NEW installed
silently over it, no uninstall; its files, its version, the Apps list), migrate (the new daemon's first start on the folder with NEOAPRS_NO_DEVICES=1 too: the migration and its copy in the log, nothing ERROR),
data (`db radios`, `db list`, `db restore`, `db stations` and `doctor` of the new release, held here to what the old one said: the settings that kept their names, radio 1 and radio 2 made of the flat keys,
exactly one copy premigrate-v<the old schema version> marked as taken before the update, every station kept, no FAIL), daemon (a second start: page, no ERROR or Traceback, stations of the old run heard again,
nothing migrated) and uninstall (as the install proof's). The data folder is the run's own (data-upgrade), never the default one. The commands of old and station are those of 0.18.2 (v0.18.2:neoaprs/cli/dbcmd.py,
neoaprs/daemon.py build_parser, neoaprs/cli/stopcmd.py); a release before that is older than 0.18.2 may take other ones.

What only a person can see (the wizard, the tray at each display scaling, the pages of the app, Update now from the previous release) is in docs/development.md.

Exit code: 0 all steps passed, 1 a step failed, 2 not set up (a variable, a file, a program on the PATH, a tree that cannot be packed, a machine that is in no state to be used, a second run, the
machine not answering, uv or the tree not put on it). Needs Linux, ssh, scp, VBoxManage and git."""
import argparse
import base64
import contextlib
import fcntl
import hashlib
import importlib.machinery
import importlib.util
import os
import re
import shutil
import signal
import subprocess
import sys
import tarfile
import tempfile
import time
from collections.abc import Callable, Iterator, Mapping, Sequence
from dataclasses import dataclass
from pathlib import Path
from types import FrameType, ModuleType
from typing import NamedTuple

SCRIPTS = Path(__file__).resolve().parent
ROOT = SCRIPTS.parent
NOT_SET_UP = 2
LOOPBACK = "127.0.0.1"
KEEP_RUNS = 2                                          # the folders of runs left on the machine: this run's and the one before
TAIL_LINES = 40                                        # of a failed step's output under its line
SSH_PATIENCE_SEC = 300.0                               # a Windows that was powered off answers SSH after a minute or two
SETTLED_SEC = 120.0                                    # how long a Windows this run started must have been up before the steps begin: it restarts its SSH service once in its first minute, and a step in that moment ends with "closed by remote host"
UPTIME_SCRIPT = "[int]((Get-Date) - (Get-CimInstance Win32_OperatingSystem).LastBootUpTime).TotalSeconds; exit 0"
OFF_PATIENCE_SEC = 300.0                               # and shuts down in about as long
REMOTE_LINE_MAX = 8000                                 # cmd.exe, which may be the machine's SSH shell, takes 8191 characters of a command line
NEVER_STOPS = float("inf")
SHUTDOWN_SCRIPT = "shutdown.exe /s /t 0 /f; exit 0"     # Windows's own shutdown, at once; programs that would hold it are closed (the machine is a test machine and the run is over)


class Pin(NamedTuple):
    version: str
    url: str
    sha256: str
    file: str


# uv for Windows, from the release of its own repository, kept only when its SHA-256 is this one (the pin is the trust, not the server); the same version as the one the Linux machine runs.
UV = Pin("0.11.26", "https://github.com/astral-sh/uv/releases/download/0.11.26/uv-x86_64-pc-windows-msvc.zip",
         "4e1278ede866be6c0bf32d2f466cc6de7a9fb399ecf20c9ce2d186e52424be47", "uv-x86_64-pc-windows-msvc.zip")

VARIABLES = ("NEOAPRS_WINVM_SSH_PORT", "NEOAPRS_WINVM_SSH_KEY", "NEOAPRS_WINVM_KNOWN_HOSTS")
# The Python of the steps is the one the workflow names (setup-uv's `python-version`, which it hands to uv as UV_PYTHON): left to uv, a clean machine gets the newest Python the project allows, which is
# not what GitHub runs (seen on 14 November 2026: 3.14 on the clean machine, 3.13 in the workflow). tests/test_check_windows.py holds it to ci.yml.
PYTHON = "3.13"
STEP_ENVIRONMENT = {"NEOAPRS_NO_DEVICES": "1", "NEOAPRS_UPDATE_CHECK": "0", "UV_PYTHON_PREFERENCE": "only-managed", "UV_PYTHON": PYTHON}
NEEDS_THE_ENVIRONMENT = ("ruff", "pytest")             # the steps that run in the .venv that sync makes


def say(text: str) -> None:
    print(f"check-windows: {text}", file=sys.stderr, flush=True)


class NotSetUp(Exception):
    """Why the check cannot run, as the sentence the user is told (exit code 2)."""


def load_script(name: str) -> ModuleType:
    """A tool of this folder that has no .py in its name, run as a module so that its functions can be used."""
    loader = importlib.machinery.SourceFileLoader(name.replace("-", "_"), str(SCRIPTS / name))
    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_loader(loader.name, loader)
    assert spec is not None
    module = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)
    loader.exec_module(module)
    return module


# ---- where the machine is ----

@dataclass(frozen=True)
class Settings:
    vm: str
    port: int
    key: Path
    known_hosts: Path
    user: str


def read_settings(env: Mapping[str, str]) -> Settings:
    """The machine as the environment names it, or NotSetUp with the sentence. Nothing has a default but the user."""
    vm = env.get("NEOAPRS_WINVM", "").strip()
    if not vm:
        raise NotSetUp("the Windows check is not set up on this machine: it needs NEOAPRS_WINVM (the VirtualBox name of the Windows machine), NEOAPRS_WINVM_SSH_PORT, NEOAPRS_WINVM_SSH_KEY and "
                       "NEOAPRS_WINVM_KNOWN_HOSTS, and NEOAPRS_WINVM_USER when the user there is not John")
    if vm.startswith("-"):
        raise NotSetUp(f"NEOAPRS_WINVM is {vm!r}, which VBoxManage would read as an option: the name of the machine does not begin with a dash")
    missing = [name for name in VARIABLES if not env.get(name, "").strip()]
    if missing:
        raise NotSetUp(f"NEOAPRS_WINVM is set, and {' and '.join(missing)} {'is' if len(missing) == 1 else 'are'} not")
    port_text = env["NEOAPRS_WINVM_SSH_PORT"].strip()
    if not port_text.isascii() or not port_text.isdigit() or not 0 < int(port_text) < 65536:
        raise NotSetUp(f"NEOAPRS_WINVM_SSH_PORT is {port_text!r}, which is not a port number")
    user = env.get("NEOAPRS_WINVM_USER", "").strip() or "John"
    if not re.fullmatch(r"[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]*", user):
        raise NotSetUp(f"NEOAPRS_WINVM_USER is {user!r}: a user name here is letters, digits, dots, dashes and underscores")
    known_hosts = env["NEOAPRS_WINVM_KNOWN_HOSTS"].strip()
    if '"' in known_hosts:
        raise NotSetUp("NEOAPRS_WINVM_KNOWN_HOSTS has a double quote in it, which ssh cannot be given in an option")
    return Settings(vm, int(port_text), Path(env["NEOAPRS_WINVM_SSH_KEY"].strip()), Path(known_hosts), user)


def missing_files(settings: Settings) -> list[str]:
    """The sentences for the files that are not there: the key and the known_hosts file."""
    return [f"{name} is {path}, which is not a file" for name, path in (("NEOAPRS_WINVM_SSH_KEY", settings.key), ("NEOAPRS_WINVM_KNOWN_HOSTS", settings.known_hosts)) if not path.is_file()]


def build_cache(env: Mapping[str, str]) -> Path:
    """The build cache, where scripts/security-tools keeps its programs: the zip of uv and the lock files are here too."""
    base = env.get("NEOAPRS_BUILD_CACHE") or Path(env.get("XDG_CACHE_HOME") or Path.home() / ".cache") / "neoaprs-build"
    return Path(base) / "check-windows"


# ---- command lines ----

def option_value(path: Path) -> str:
    """A path as the value of an ssh option: in double quotes when it has a space, which ssh's own parser takes apart."""
    text = str(path)
    return f'"{text}"' if any(char.isspace() for char in text) else text


def ssh_options(settings: Settings) -> list[str]:
    """What ssh and scp share: the key and only that key, no question asked (a host key that is not in the file is a refusal), and an unanswered connection given up on."""
    return ["-i", str(settings.key), "-o", "IdentitiesOnly=yes", "-o", "BatchMode=yes", "-o", f"UserKnownHostsFile={option_value(settings.known_hosts)}",
            "-o", "ConnectTimeout=10", "-o", "ServerAliveInterval=15"]


def ssh_command(settings: Settings, remote: str, tty: bool = False) -> list[str]:
    """ssh with the command line that the machine's shell runs. `tty` (-tt) gives it a console even though this side has none."""
    return ["ssh", *ssh_options(settings), "-p", str(settings.port), *(["-tt"] if tty else []), f"{settings.user}@{LOOPBACK}", remote]


def scp_command(settings: Settings, local: Path, remote_path: str) -> list[str]:
    """scp of one file to a path on the machine, which is written with forward slashes (C:/Users/...)."""
    return ["scp", *ssh_options(settings), "-P", str(settings.port), str(local), f"{settings.user}@{LOOPBACK}:{remote_path}"]


def ps_quote(text: str) -> str:
    """A PowerShell string in single quotes. PowerShell takes the typographic single quotes for quotes too, so each of them is doubled as the plain one is."""
    return "'" + "".join(char * 2 if char in "'\u2018\u2019\u201a\u201b" else char for char in text) + "'"


class Raw(str):
    """A piece of a PowerShell command that is an expression and is not quoted."""


def encode_powershell(script: str) -> str:
    return base64.b64encode(script.encode("utf-16-le")).decode("ascii")


def powershell_line(script: str) -> str:
    """The command line that runs a script on the machine whichever shell sshd starts (cmd.exe or PowerShell): the script in Base64, so that no quote of it is read by that shell. The execution
    policy is bypassed only for this line: -EncodedCommand is not a script file, but a machine of a stricter policy would still say so."""
    return f"powershell.exe -NoProfile -NonInteractive -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -OutputFormat Text -EncodedCommand {encode_powershell(script)}"


def ssh_script(settings: Settings, script: str, tty: bool = False) -> list[str]:
    return ssh_command(settings, powershell_line(script), tty)


class Paths(NamedTuple):
    """Where things are on the machine, Windows paths (the profile folder is C:\\Users\\USER)."""
    home: str
    root: str          # the folders of the runs
    run: str
    tree: str          # the tree, a repository when git is there
    tar: str
    uv_dir: str
    uv_zip: str


def windows_paths(user: str, run_name: str) -> Paths:
    home = f"C:\\Users\\{user}"
    root = f"{home}\\neoaprs-check"
    run = f"{root}\\{run_name}"
    return Paths(home, root, run, f"{run}\\neoaprs", f"{run}-tree.tar", f"{home}\\neotest\\uv", f"{root}\\{UV.file}")


def scp_path(windows_path: str) -> str:
    return windows_path.replace("\\", "/")


def run_name(now: float) -> str:
    """The folder of a run: its UTC time, which sorts as time does."""
    return time.strftime("RUN-%Y%m%dT%H%M%S", time.gmtime(now))


RUN_NAME = re.compile(r"RUN-\d{8}T\d{6}")


def runs_to_remove(names: Sequence[str], keep: int = KEEP_RUNS) -> list[str]:
    """Of the folders found, the names of runs but the newest `keep`, oldest first; whatever else is in the folder is not ours and stays."""
    runs = sorted(name.strip() for name in names if RUN_NAME.fullmatch(name.strip()))
    return runs[: max(0, len(runs) - keep)]


def native(program: str, *arguments: str) -> list[str]:
    """The lines of a PowerShell script that run a program and pass its output on as text (its error stream is merged: Windows PowerShell 5.1 turns what a program writes to it into error records,
    which `"$_"` makes lines again) and end the script with its exit code when it is not 0."""
    call = "& " + " ".join(argument if isinstance(argument, Raw) else ps_quote(argument) for argument in (program, *arguments))
    return [f'{call} 2>&1 | ForEach-Object {{ "$_" }}', "if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { exit $LASTEXITCODE }"]


# GitHub's Windows runner has the programs of Git for Windows on its PATH, sh and bash among them, and tests start them (tests/test_install_line.py reads a script with `sh -n`). An SSH session
# gets git's own folder only (Git\cmd), so the folder of sh and bash is added where it is there; a machine without Git for Windows runs as it is, and those tests fail there by name.
GIT_TOOLS_ON_THE_PATH = "$gitBin = Join-Path $env:ProgramFiles 'Git\\bin'; if (Test-Path -LiteralPath $gitBin) { $env:Path = $env:Path + ';' + $gitBin }"


def preamble(paths: Paths, frozen: bool = True, folder: str | None = None) -> list[str]:
    """The start of a step's script: the environment of every step, uv first on the PATH, and the folder of the tree. A failure here ends the script; what comes after it is the program's own."""
    lines = ["$ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'", "$ProgressPreference = 'SilentlyContinue'"]
    lines += [f"$env:{name} = {ps_quote(value)}" for name, value in STEP_ENVIRONMENT.items()]
    lines.append("$env:UV_FROZEN = '1'" if frozen else "Remove-Item Env:UV_FROZEN -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue")
    lines += [f"$env:Path = {ps_quote(paths.uv_dir + ';')} + $env:Path", GIT_TOOLS_ON_THE_PATH, f"Set-Location -LiteralPath {ps_quote(folder or paths.tree)}", "$ErrorActionPreference = 'Continue'"]
    return lines


@dataclass(frozen=True)
class Step:
    name: str
    commands: tuple[tuple[str, ...], ...]      # each one a program and its arguments, run one after the other until one fails
    frozen: bool = True                        # UV_FROZEN=1, as the workflow has it
    timeout_sec: float = 900.0


def steps(paths: Paths, pytest_args: Sequence[str] = ()) -> list[Step]:
    """The steps in order: the commands of ci.yml's jobs `python` (without mypy, which the workflow runs on Linux only) and `smoke`, which tests/test_check_windows.py reads against the workflow."""
    venv = f"{paths.run}\\smoke-venv"
    python, command = f"{venv}\\Scripts\\python.exe", f"{venv}\\Scripts\\neoaprs.exe"
    wheel = Raw("(Get-ChildItem -LiteralPath 'dist' -Filter '*.whl').FullName")
    return [
        Step("sync", (("uv", "sync", "--frozen", "--extra", "app", "--extra", "ble"),)),
        Step("lock", (("uv", "lock", "--check"),), frozen=False, timeout_sec=300.0),
        Step("ruff", (("uv", "run", "ruff", "check", "."),), timeout_sec=300.0),
        Step("pytest", (("uv", "run", "pytest", "-n", "auto", "-p", "no:cacheprovider", *pytest_args),), timeout_sec=2400.0),
        Step("smoke", (("uv", "build", "--wheel"), ("uv", "venv", venv), ("uv", "pip", "install", "--python", python, wheel), (python, "scripts\\smoke.py", "--command", command))),
    ]


def step_script(paths: Paths, step: Step) -> str:
    lines = preamble(paths, step.frozen)
    for command in step.commands:
        lines += native(*command)
    return "\n".join([*lines, "exit 0"])


def chosen_steps(only: Sequence[str]) -> list[str]:
    """The names to run, in the order of the CI: all when none is chosen; sync joins ruff and pytest, which run in what it makes."""
    names = list(only) or [step.name for step in steps(windows_paths("x", "x"))]
    if any(name in names for name in NEEDS_THE_ENVIRONMENT) and "sync" not in names:
        names.append("sync")
    return [step.name for step in steps(windows_paths("x", "x")) if step.name in names]


# The probe of the console: a child in a process group of its own, Ctrl+Break sent to it, which must end it (what tests/support/proc.py does). Run by the Python of the environment.
CONSOLE_PROBE = ("import signal,subprocess,sys,time; p=subprocess.Popen([sys.executable,'-c','import time; time.sleep(60)'],creationflags=subprocess.CREATE_NEW_PROCESS_GROUP); time.sleep(1); "
                 "p.send_signal(signal.CTRL_BREAK_EVENT); time.sleep(3); code=p.poll(); p.kill(); print('Ctrl+Break ended the child:', code is not None); sys.exit(0 if code is not None else 1)")


def probe_script(paths: Paths) -> str:
    python = f"{paths.tree}\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe"
    return "\n".join([*preamble(paths), *native(python, "-c", CONSOLE_PROBE), "exit 0"])


def stop_script(folder: str) -> str:
    """Ends every process whose command line names the folder of the run (the programs of the .venv are started by their full path): what is left of a step that was given up on."""
    return ("Get-CimInstance Win32_Process | Where-Object { $_.CommandLine -like ('*' + " + ps_quote(folder) + " + '*') -and $_.ProcessId -ne $PID } | "
            "ForEach-Object { Stop-Process -Id $_.ProcessId -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue }; exit 0")


def prepare_script(paths: Paths) -> str:
    """The folder of the run made, the tar unpacked into it and, where git is, the tree made a repository of one commit made of the tracked files. The git part is a nicety: it never fails the run."""
    tar = "$env:SystemRoot + '\\System32\\tar.exe'"
    git_lines = ["$git = Get-Command git.exe -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue",
                 "if ($git) { try {",
                 f"  Set-Location -LiteralPath {ps_quote(paths.tree)}",
                 "  & git.exe -c core.autocrlf=false init --quiet --initial-branch=master . 2>&1 | Out-Null",
                 f"  & git.exe -c core.autocrlf=false add --force --pathspec-from-file={ps_quote(paths.run + chr(92) + 'tracked')} --pathspec-file-nul 2>&1 | Out-Null",
                 "  & git.exe -c user.name=runner -c user.email=runner@localhost -c commit.gpgsign=false commit --quiet --allow-empty --message='The tree as it was on disk' 2>&1 | Out-Null",
                 "} catch { } }"]
    return "\n".join(["$ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'", "$ProgressPreference = 'SilentlyContinue'",
                      f"New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path {ps_quote(paths.root)} | Out-Null",
                      f"New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path {ps_quote(paths.run)} | Out-Null",
                      f"& ({tar}) -xf {ps_quote(paths.tar)} -C {ps_quote(paths.run)}",
                      "if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { exit $LASTEXITCODE }",
                      f"Remove-Item -LiteralPath {ps_quote(paths.tar)}",
                      "$ErrorActionPreference = 'Continue'", *git_lines, "exit 0"])


def uv_version_script(paths: Paths) -> str:
    return "\n".join(["$ErrorActionPreference = 'SilentlyContinue'", f"& {ps_quote(paths.uv_dir + chr(92) + 'uv.exe')} --version 2>&1 | ForEach-Object {{ \"$_\" }}", "exit 0"])


def uv_unpack_script(paths: Paths) -> str:
    tar = "$env:SystemRoot + '\\System32\\tar.exe'"
    return "\n".join(["$ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'", f"New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path {ps_quote(paths.uv_dir)} | Out-Null",
                      f"& ({tar}) -xf {ps_quote(paths.uv_zip)} -C {ps_quote(paths.uv_dir)}", "if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { exit $LASTEXITCODE }",
                      f"Remove-Item -LiteralPath {ps_quote(paths.uv_zip)}", "exit 0"])


def listing_script(paths: Paths) -> str:
    return f"Get-ChildItem -LiteralPath {ps_quote(paths.root)} -Directory -Name -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue; exit 0"


def removal_script(paths: Paths, names: Sequence[str]) -> str:
    """Takes the folders of old runs away; only names that are runs, and a folder that cannot be removed (something holds a file of it) is left."""
    return "\n".join([f"Remove-Item -LiteralPath {ps_quote(paths.root + chr(92) + name)} -Recurse -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue" for name in names if RUN_NAME.fullmatch(name)] + ["exit 0"])


def uv_version_ok(output: str, pin: Pin = UV) -> bool:
    """Whether what `uv --version` printed names the pinned version."""
    found = re.match(r"uv (\S+)", output.strip())
    return found is not None and found.group(1) == pin.version


# ---- the output and the result lines ----

ESCAPES = re.compile(r"\x1b\[[0-9;?]*[ -/]*[@-~]|\x1b\][^\x07\x1b]*(?:\x07|\x1b\\)|\x1b[()][A-Za-z0-9]|\x1b[=>]")


def clean_output(text: str) -> str:
    """What a session with a console adds taken away: escape sequences, the carriage returns of its line ends, and what a line wrote before a bare carriage return overwrote it."""
    lines = ESCAPES.sub("", text).replace("\r\n", "\n").split("\n")
    return "\n".join(line.rsplit("\r", 1)[-1] for line in lines)


@dataclass(frozen=True)
class StepResult:
    name: str
    code: int
    seconds: float
    log: Path
    tail: tuple[str, ...] = ()


def result_line(result: StepResult) -> str:
    """The line of scripts/check: `ok` or `FAIL`, the name, the seconds in tenths."""
    tenths = int(result.seconds * 10 + 0.5)
    return f"{'ok' if result.code == 0 else 'FAIL':<5} {result.name:<12} {tenths // 10:4d}.{tenths % 10}s"


def report_lines(result: StepResult) -> list[str]:
    """The result line, and under a failed step the end of its output and where the whole is."""
    if result.code == 0:
        return [result_line(result)]
    return [result_line(result), *(f"      | {line}" for line in result.tail), f"      (the whole log: {result.log})"]


def exit_code(results: Sequence[StepResult]) -> int:
    return 1 if any(result.code != 0 for result in results) else 0


def summary(results: Sequence[StepResult], seconds: float) -> str:
    failed = [result.name for result in results if result.code != 0]
    return f"failed in {int(seconds)}s: {' '.join(failed)}" if failed else f"all green in {int(seconds)}s"


# ---- power and the lock ----

class Refused(Exception):
    """The machine cannot be used as asked: the sentence for the user (exit code 2)."""


class Busy(Exception):
    """Another run holds the lock."""


START_FROM = ("poweroff", "aborted", "saved", "aborted-saved")


@dataclass(frozen=True)
class PowerPlan:
    restore: bool        # the snapshot is put back before the start
    start: bool          # this run starts the machine, and so shuts it down at the end


def plan_power(state: str, snapshot: str, vm: str = "the machine") -> PowerPlan:
    """What a run does about power, from the state VirtualBox gives. A running machine is used as it is and left running, and is no machine to put back to a snapshot; a machine that is off is
    started, and shut down again by the run that started it; one that is between the two is not touched."""
    if state == "running":
        if snapshot:
            raise Refused(f"--snapshot puts a machine back only while it is powered off, and {vm} is running: shut it down first")
        return PowerPlan(restore=False, start=False)
    if state in START_FROM:
        return PowerPlan(restore=bool(snapshot), start=True)
    raise Refused(f"{vm} is {state or 'in a state VBoxManage did not tell'}: it is used when it is running or powered off, so wait or finish what it does and run again")


def parse_vm_state(output: str) -> str:
    """The state from `VBoxManage showvminfo --machinereadable`: the line `VMState="running"`."""
    found = re.search(r'^VMState="([^"]*)"', output, re.MULTILINE)
    return found.group(1) if found else ""


def lock_path(env: Mapping[str, str], vm: str) -> Path:
    """The lock file of a machine: in the build cache, named by the machine's name with whatever is not a letter or a digit made a dash."""
    return build_cache(env) / "locks" / (re.sub(r"[^A-Za-z0-9._]", "-", vm) + ".lock")


@contextlib.contextmanager
def run_lock(path: Path) -> Iterator[None]:
    """One run at a time on a machine: the lock is the file's, and goes when the run ends however it ends."""
    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    with path.open("a") as handle:
        try:
            fcntl.flock(handle, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
        except BlockingIOError:
            raise Busy(f"another run of this script holds {path}: one run at a time on a machine") from None
        yield


def wait_for(done: Callable[[], bool], patience_sec: float, interval_sec: float = 5.0, sleep: Callable[[float], None] = time.sleep, clock: Callable[[], float] = time.monotonic) -> bool:
    """Asks `done` until it says yes (True) or the patience is over (False)."""
    deadline = clock() + patience_sec
    while not done():
        if clock() >= deadline:
            return False
        sleep(interval_sec)
    return True


def vboxmanage(*arguments: str) -> subprocess.CompletedProcess[str]:
    return subprocess.run(["VBoxManage", *arguments], capture_output=True, text=True)


def vm_state(vm: str) -> str:
    return parse_vm_state(vboxmanage("showvminfo", vm, "--machinereadable").stdout)


def last_line(text: str) -> str:
    return (text.strip().splitlines() or ["it said nothing"])[-1]


def start_vm(settings: Settings, plan: PowerPlan, snapshot: str) -> None:
    """The snapshot put back when asked, then the machine started without a window, and waited for until its SSH answers."""
    if plan.restore:
        say(f"putting {settings.vm} back to the snapshot {snapshot}")
        done = vboxmanage("snapshot", settings.vm, "restore", snapshot)
        if done.returncode != 0:
            raise Refused(f"the snapshot {snapshot} could not be put back ({last_line(done.stderr or done.stdout)})")
    say(f"starting {settings.vm} without a window")
    done = vboxmanage("startvm", settings.vm, "--type", "headless")
    if done.returncode != 0:
        raise Refused(f"{settings.vm} could not be started ({last_line(done.stderr or done.stdout)})")


def ssh_answers(settings: Settings) -> bool:
    return subprocess.run(ssh_script(settings, "exit 0"), stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, capture_output=True).returncode == 0


def wait_for_ssh(settings: Settings, patience_sec: float = SSH_PATIENCE_SEC, interval_sec: float = 5.0) -> None:
    say(f"waiting for the SSH of {settings.vm} to answer (up to {int(patience_sec)} s)")
    if not wait_for(lambda: ssh_answers(settings), patience_sec, interval_sec):
        raise Refused(f"the SSH of {settings.vm} did not answer within {int(patience_sec)} s (port {settings.port}, user {settings.user}): is the machine's forward and its sshd right? try the ssh line by hand")


def uptime_sec(settings: Settings) -> float | None:
    """How long the machine has been up, by its own word; None when it could not be asked (its SSH is away), and endless when its answer is no number (nothing to wait for is known)."""
    done = ssh_run(settings, UPTIME_SCRIPT, timeout_sec=60.0)
    if done.returncode != 0:
        return None
    words = done.stdout.split()
    return float(words[-1]) if words and words[-1].isdigit() else NEVER_STOPS


def wait_until_settled(settings: Settings, patience_sec: float = SSH_PATIENCE_SEC, interval_sec: float = 5.0) -> None:
    """For a machine this run has just started: waits until it has been up for SETTLED_SEC, so that no step meets the restart of its SSH service (seen twice on 14 November 2026: the first step after the
    boot ended with "Connection closed by remote host" ten seconds after the SSH had first answered)."""
    def settled() -> bool:
        up = uptime_sec(settings)
        return up is not None and up >= SETTLED_SEC
    first = uptime_sec(settings)
    if first is not None and first >= SETTLED_SEC:
        return
    say(f"{settings.vm} has just started: waiting until it has been up for {int(SETTLED_SEC)} s")
    if not wait_for(settled, patience_sec, interval_sec):
        raise Refused(f"{settings.vm} did not say how long it has been up within {int(patience_sec)} s: its SSH comes and goes")


def power_off(settings: Settings, patience_sec: float = OFF_PATIENCE_SEC, interval_sec: float = 5.0) -> None:
    """The machine shut down by Windows itself and waited for: asked from inside over SSH (`shutdown.exe /s`), and when that has not turned it off, by the ACPI power button. (The button alone was not
    enough: a Windows that nobody is looking at did nothing with it for two minutes, 13 November 2026.) Never a hard power-off: one that is not off in time is left as it is, and said."""
    say(f"shutting {settings.vm} down")
    ssh_run(settings, SHUTDOWN_SCRIPT, timeout_sec=60.0)
    if wait_for(lambda: vm_state(settings.vm) == "poweroff", patience_sec, interval_sec):
        return
    vboxmanage("controlvm", settings.vm, "acpipowerbutton")
    if wait_for(lambda: vm_state(settings.vm) == "poweroff", patience_sec, interval_sec):
        return
    say(f"{settings.vm} is not powered off after {int(patience_sec)} s: left as it is, shut it down by hand")


# ---- the machine ----

def ssh_run(settings: Settings, script: str, timeout_sec: float = 300.0) -> subprocess.CompletedProcess[str]:
    """A short script on the machine, its output as text. An answer that does not come is a failed one."""
    try:
        return subprocess.run(ssh_script(settings, script), stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, capture_output=True, text=True, errors="replace", timeout=timeout_sec)
    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired as error:
        return subprocess.CompletedProcess(error.cmd, 124, "", f"no answer within {int(timeout_sec)} s")


def ensure_uv_zip(cache: Path, pin: Pin = UV, download: Callable[[str, Path, str], None] | None = None) -> Path:
    """The zip of uv in the build cache: the one there when its digest is the pin's, else fetched (from GitHub's hosts only, by scripts/security-tools's own download, which checks the digest)."""
    target = cache / f"uv-{pin.version}" / pin.file
    with contextlib.suppress(OSError):
        if hashlib.sha256(target.read_bytes()).hexdigest() == pin.sha256:
            return target
    fetch = download or load_script("security-tools").download
    target.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    part = target.with_name(target.name + ".part")
    try:
        fetch(pin.url, part, pin.sha256)
        part.replace(target)
    finally:
        part.unlink(missing_ok=True)
    return target


def copy_to(settings: Settings, local: Path, remote_windows_path: str) -> None:
    done = subprocess.run(scp_command(settings, local, scp_path(remote_windows_path)), stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, capture_output=True, text=True, errors="replace")
    if done.returncode != 0:
        raise Refused(f"{local.name} could not be copied to the machine ({last_line(done.stderr)})")


def remote_must(settings: Settings, script: str, failure: str) -> None:
    done = ssh_run(settings, script)
    if done.returncode != 0:
        raise Refused(f"{failure} ({last_line(done.stdout + done.stderr)})")


def make_root(settings: Settings, paths: Paths) -> None:
    """The folder of the runs on the machine, made when it is not there: the zip of uv and the tree are copied into it, and a clean machine has none (scp makes no folder)."""
    remote_must(settings, f"$ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'; New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path {ps_quote(paths.root)} | Out-Null; exit 0", "the folder for the runs could not be made")


def put_uv_there(settings: Settings, paths: Paths, cache: Path) -> None:
    """uv of the pinned version in its folder on the machine: left alone when it is there, else the zip is copied over and unpacked."""
    if uv_version_ok(ssh_run(settings, uv_version_script(paths)).stdout):
        return
    say(f"putting uv {UV.version} on the machine")
    try:
        zip_file = ensure_uv_zip(cache)
    except Exception as error:      # (what the download says: the pin, the network or the disk; the sentence is the user's)
        raise Refused(f"uv {UV.version} could not be fetched ({error})") from None
    make_root(settings, paths)
    copy_to(settings, zip_file, paths.uv_zip)
    remote_must(settings, uv_unpack_script(paths), "uv could not be unpacked on the machine")
    if not uv_version_ok(ssh_run(settings, uv_version_script(paths)).stdout):
        raise Refused(f"uv {UV.version} is not what runs from {paths.uv_dir} after it was put there")


def prepare(settings: Settings, paths: Paths, tar: Path, cache: Path) -> None:
    """The machine made ready for the steps: uv, then the tree in the folder of the run."""
    put_uv_there(settings, paths, cache)
    say(f"copying the tree to {paths.run}")
    make_root(settings, paths)
    copy_to(settings, tar, paths.tar)
    remote_must(settings, prepare_script(paths), "the tree could not be unpacked on the machine")


def remove_old_runs(settings: Settings, paths: Paths) -> None:
    """The folders of older runs taken away but the newest two. What cannot be done is only logged: it is a courtesy to the disk of the machine."""
    names = runs_to_remove(ssh_run(settings, listing_script(paths)).stdout.splitlines())
    if names:
        say(f"removing the older runs on the machine: {' '.join(names)}")
        ssh_run(settings, removal_script(paths, names), timeout_sec=900.0)


def run_step(settings: Settings, paths: Paths, step: Step, log_dir: Path, tty: bool = False) -> StepResult:
    """One step on the machine, its whole output in a log here. A step that is not done in its time is ended, with what it left on the machine, and fails with code 124."""
    return run_script(settings, paths, step.name, step_script(paths, step), step.timeout_sec, log_dir, tty)


def run_script(settings: Settings, paths: Paths, name: str, script: str, timeout_sec: float, log_dir: Path, tty: bool = False) -> StepResult:
    """A step's script on the machine: what run_step does, for any script."""
    log = log_dir / f"{name}.log"
    say(f"running {name}")
    started = time.monotonic()
    code, note = 0, ""
    with log.open("wb") as out:
        proc = subprocess.Popen(ssh_script(settings, script, tty), stdin=subprocess.PIPE if tty else subprocess.DEVNULL, stdout=out, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT)
        try:
            code = proc.wait(timeout=timeout_sec)
        except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
            code, note = 124, f"(stopped: the step did not end in {int(timeout_sec)} s)"
            proc.kill()
            proc.wait()
            ssh_run(settings, stop_script(paths.run), timeout_sec=60.0)
        except BaseException:
            proc.kill()
            proc.wait()
            ssh_run(settings, stop_script(paths.run), timeout_sec=60.0)
            raise
        finally:
            if proc.stdin is not None:
                proc.stdin.close()
    text = clean_output(log.read_bytes().decode("utf-8", errors="replace"))
    log.write_text(text + (note and "\n" + note) + "\n", encoding="utf-8")
    tail = [*text.rstrip("\n").splitlines()[-TAIL_LINES:], *([note] if note else [])]
    return StepResult(name, code, time.monotonic() - started, log, tuple(tail))


def console_works(settings: Settings, paths: Paths, tty: bool) -> bool:
    """Whether the probe ends its child with Ctrl+Break in a session of this kind."""
    with subprocess.Popen(ssh_script(settings, probe_script(paths), tty), stdin=subprocess.PIPE if tty else subprocess.DEVNULL, stdout=subprocess.DEVNULL, stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL) as proc:
        try:
            return proc.wait(timeout=120) == 0
        finally:
            proc.kill()                      # (a probe that hangs is a failed one; its input, held open for a console, closes when the with block ends)


def choose_console(settings: Settings, paths: Paths, force_tty: bool) -> bool:
    """Whether the pytest step runs through `ssh -tt`: when asked, or when a plain session cannot send Ctrl+Break and one with a console can. Said either way."""
    if force_tty:
        return True
    try:
        if console_works(settings, paths, tty=False):
            say("Ctrl+Break reaches a child in a plain SSH session: pytest runs in one")
            return False
        if console_works(settings, paths, tty=True):
            say("Ctrl+Break does not reach a child in a plain SSH session, and does in one with a console: pytest runs through ssh -tt")
            return True
    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
        pass
    say("the probe of Ctrl+Break did not pass in either kind of session: pytest runs in a plain one, and the tests that end a child that way will fail")
    return False


def execute(settings: Settings, names: Sequence[str], pytest_args: Sequence[str], tar: Path, cache: Path, force_tty: bool) -> int:
    """From a machine that answers to the last result line; every step runs to its end except that none follows a failed sync."""
    paths = windows_paths(settings.user, run_name(time.time()))
    log_dir = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="neoaprs-check-windows-"))
    say(f"the logs are in {log_dir}")
    prepare(settings, paths, tar, cache)
    results: list[StepResult] = []
    total = time.monotonic()
    tty = False
    try:
        for step in steps(paths, pytest_args):
            if step.name not in names:
                continue
            if step.name == "sync" or "sync" not in [result.name for result in results if result.code != 0]:
                if step.name == "pytest":
                    tty = choose_console(settings, paths, force_tty)
                result = run_step(settings, paths, step, log_dir, tty and step.name == "pytest")
                results.append(result)
                print("\n".join(report_lines(result)), flush=True)
    finally:
        remove_old_runs(settings, paths)
    print(summary(results, time.monotonic() - total), flush=True)
    return exit_code(results)


# ---- the install proof (--install) ----

# The scripted part of the Windows proof (docs/development.md, "The clean install"): the installer run silently on a machine put back to its clean snapshot, then the pieces of the app that pull modules and
# DLLs nothing else does, each a step with its result line, the uninstall last. The steps before `smoke` run on a machine that has nothing but Windows and the installed app: uv and its Python come only for
# the two smoke scripts, which need a Python, and they go into folders of their own, never on the PATH of the app.
INSTALLER_NAME = re.compile(r"NeoAPRS-Setup-(\d+\.\d+\.\d+(?:-[0-9A-Za-z]+)?)\.exe")
INSTALL_STEP_NAMES = ("install", "defender", "daemon", "commands", "app", "map", "direwolf", "smoke", "mercury", "uninstall")
NEEDS_PYTHON = ("smoke", "mercury")
# What each program says it is (its FileDescription, which Task Manager shows): packaging/windows/neoaprs.spec; tests/test_check_windows.py holds the two to it.
DESCRIPTIONS = {"neoaprsw": "NeoAPRS, the APRS client that runs in the background", "neoaprs-app": "NeoAPRS, the window and the tray icon"}
# The files the smoke steps run, at their places in the tree: scripts/smoke.py with the capture its fake TNC plays, and the check of Mercury's ports.
KIT = ("scripts/smoke.py", "tests/fixtures/kiss/thd7-2026-10-21.bin", "packaging/windows/smoke_mercury.py")
APP_FOLDER = "$app = Join-Path $env:LOCALAPPDATA 'Programs\\NeoAPRS'"
DATA_FOLDER = "$data = Join-Path $env:LOCALAPPDATA 'NeoAPRS'"
# A PowerShell function: the page's address from a log once the daemon has written it (`web page at http://...`), or nothing when the process ended or the time is over.
WAIT_PAGE = """function Wait-Page([string]$log, $process, [int]$seconds) {
  foreach ($i in 1..$seconds) {
    $m = if (Test-Path -LiteralPath $log) { Select-String -LiteralPath $log -Pattern 'web page at (http://\\S+/)' | Select-Object -Last 1 }
    if ($m) { return $m.Matches[0].Groups[1].Value }
    if ($process.HasExited) { return $null }
    Start-Sleep 1
  }
  return $null
}"""


class InstallPaths(NamedTuple):
    """Where the install proof keeps things on the machine, all in the folder of the run."""
    setup: str
    install_log: str
    uninstall_log: str
    kit: str
    kit_tar: str
    data_app: str
    data_map: str
    data_direwolf: str
    support: str


def install_paths(paths: Paths, installer_name: str) -> InstallPaths:
    run = paths.run
    return InstallPaths(f"{run}\\{installer_name}", f"{run}\\install.log", f"{run}\\uninstall.log", f"{run}\\kit", f"{run}-kit.tar", f"{run}\\data-app", f"{run}\\data-map", f"{run}\\data-direwolf", f"{run}\\support")


def installer_version(installer: Path, option: str = "--install") -> str:
    """The version the installer's name says (NeoAPRS-Setup-0.20.0.exe), or NotSetUp with the sentence."""
    found = INSTALLER_NAME.fullmatch(installer.name)
    if not installer.is_file() or found is None:
        raise NotSetUp(f"{option} takes the installer the release workflow makes, NeoAPRS-Setup-VERSION.exe, and {installer} is not one")
    return found.group(1)


def tornado_pin(pyproject: str) -> str:
    """The Tornado the project pins: scripts/smoke.py's WebSocket client is run with it."""
    found = re.search(r'"tornado==([^"]+)"', pyproject)
    if found is None:
        raise NotSetUp("pyproject.toml pins no tornado, which scripts/smoke.py runs with")
    return found.group(1)


def direwolf_banner(module: str) -> str:
    """What the Direwolf NeoAPRS ships says first when it runs (neoaprs/direwolf.py: BANNER with VERSION): the install proof asks the installed direwolf.exe for it."""
    version, banner = re.search(r'^VERSION = "([^"]+)"', module, re.M), re.search(r'^BANNER = "([^"]+)"', module, re.M)
    if version is None or banner is None or banner.group(1).count("%d") != 3:
        raise NotSetUp("neoaprs/direwolf.py names no VERSION and BANNER of the Direwolf NeoAPRS ships")
    return banner.group(1).replace("%d.%d.%d", version.group(1))


def pack_kit(root: Path, out: Path) -> None:
    """The tar of the files the smoke steps run, under the names they have in the tree."""
    with tarfile.open(out, "w") as tar:
        for name in KIT:
            tar.add(root / name, arcname=name, recursive=False)


def install_script(name: str, *lines: str) -> str:
    """A step of the install proof: the line that names it, no variable of a developer's (the app runs as an operator's would), the app's folder in $app."""
    return "\n".join([f"# step: {name}", "$ErrorActionPreference = 'Continue'", "$ProgressPreference = 'SilentlyContinue'", APP_FOLDER, *lines, "exit 0"])


def fail_unless(condition: str, why: str, *before: str) -> str:
    """The PowerShell line that ends the step with 1 and says why when the condition does not hold (what `before` names is run first: a log's end)."""
    return f"if (-not ({condition})) {{ {'; '.join([*before, ps_quote(why)])}; exit 1 }}"


NATIVE_OK = "$LASTEXITCODE -eq 0"
# The files of the program folder that the proofs look for after an install (packaging/windows/neoaprs.spec and neoaprs.iss put them there).
INSTALLED_FILES = ("neoaprs.exe", "neoaprsw.exe", "neoaprs-app.exe", "bin\\mercury\\mercury.exe", "bin\\direwolf\\direwolf.exe", "bin\\direwolf\\data\\tocalls.yaml", "_internal\\neoaprs\\maps\\basemap-world.pmtiles",
                   "_internal\\neoaprs\\desktop\\icon.ico", "LICENSE.txt", "unins000.exe")
START_MENU = "Join-Path $env:APPDATA 'Microsoft\\Windows\\Start Menu\\Programs\\NeoAPRS'"


def setup_lines(setup: str, log: str) -> list[str]:
    """The installer run silently, as the release's users and Update now run it, and waited for; a setup that does not end with 0 ends the step with the end of its log."""
    return [f"$setup = {ps_quote(setup)}",
            f"$p = Start-Process -FilePath $setup -ArgumentList '/VERYSILENT', '/SUPPRESSMSGBOXES', '/NORESTART', {ps_quote('/LOG=' + log)} -PassThru",
            "$p.WaitForExit()",
            fail_unless("$p.ExitCode -eq 0", "setup did not end with 0", f"Get-Content -LiteralPath {ps_quote(log)} -Tail 40", '"setup ended with $($p.ExitCode)"')]


def files_lines(files: Sequence[str]) -> list[str]:
    return [fail_unless(f"Test-Path -LiteralPath (Join-Path $app {ps_quote(f)})", f"{f} is not in the program folder") for f in files]


def version_lines(version: str) -> list[str]:
    """`neoaprs.exe --version` of the program folder, which must say this version."""
    return ["$said = (& (Join-Path $app 'neoaprs.exe') --version 2>&1 | ForEach-Object { \"$_\" } | Out-String).Trim()",
            "\"neoaprs.exe --version: $said\"",
            fail_unless(f"$said -eq {ps_quote('NeoAPRS ' + version)}", f"neoaprs.exe is not NeoAPRS {version}")]


def uninstall_script(log: str) -> str:
    """The uninstall with the app running on the default data folder: the program folder gone, nothing left in it, the start at sign-in and the processes gone, the data folder kept."""
    return install_script(
        "uninstall", DATA_FOLDER, "$log = Join-Path $data 'neoaprs.log'",
        "$before = @(Select-String -LiteralPath $log -Pattern 'NeoAPRS is running' -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue).Count",
        "$running = Start-Process -FilePath (Join-Path $app 'neoaprs-app.exe') -ArgumentList '--tray' -PassThru",
        "foreach ($i in 1..120) { if (@(Select-String -LiteralPath $log -Pattern 'NeoAPRS is running' -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue).Count -gt $before) { break }; Start-Sleep 1 }",
        fail_unless("-not $running.HasExited", "the app did not stay up before the uninstall"),
        f"$u = Start-Process -FilePath (Join-Path $app 'unins000.exe') -ArgumentList '/VERYSILENT', '/SUPPRESSMSGBOXES', '/NORESTART', {ps_quote('/LOG=' + log)} -PassThru",
        "$u.WaitForExit()",
        "foreach ($i in 1..120) { if (-not (Test-Path -LiteralPath (Join-Path $app 'neoaprs.exe'))) { break }; Start-Sleep 1 }",
        fail_unless("-not (Test-Path -LiteralPath (Join-Path $app 'neoaprs.exe'))", "neoaprs.exe is still in the program folder", f"Get-Content -LiteralPath {ps_quote(log)} -Tail 40"),
        "foreach ($i in 1..30) { if (-not (Test-Path -LiteralPath $app)) { break }; Start-Sleep 1 }",
        "$left = if (Test-Path -LiteralPath $app) { @(Get-ChildItem -LiteralPath $app -Recurse -Force | ForEach-Object { $_.FullName }) } else { @() }",
        fail_unless("$left.Count -eq 0", "the uninstall left files in the program folder", "$left"),
        fail_unless("-not (Get-ItemProperty 'HKCU:\\Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Run' -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue).NeoAPRS", "the start at sign-in is still set"),
        fail_unless("-not (Get-Process -Name neoaprs, neoaprsw, neoaprs-app -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue)", "a NeoAPRS process is still running"),
        fail_unless("Test-Path -LiteralPath (Join-Path $data 'neoaprs.sqlite')", "the data folder was touched"),
        fail_unless(f"-not (Test-Path -LiteralPath (Join-Path ({START_MENU}) 'NeoAPRS.lnk'))", "the Start menu entry is still there"),
        "'uninstalled: the program folder is gone, the data folder is still there'",
    )


def install_steps(paths: Paths, installer_name: str, version: str, tornado: str, direwolf: str) -> list[tuple[str, str, float]]:
    """The steps of the proof in order, each its name, its script and its time."""
    ip = install_paths(paths, installer_name)
    native_ok = NATIVE_OK
    entries = ("NeoAPRS", "Stop NeoAPRS", "NeoAPRS support logs")
    menu = START_MENU
    install = install_script(
        "install",
        *setup_lines(ip.setup, ip.install_log),
        *files_lines(INSTALLED_FILES),
        f"$menu = {menu}",
        *(fail_unless(f"Test-Path -LiteralPath (Join-Path $menu {ps_quote(e + '.lnk')})", f"the Start menu has no entry {e}") for e in entries),
        "$size = (Get-ChildItem -LiteralPath $app -Recurse -File | Measure-Object -Property Length -Sum).Sum",
        "$count = @(Get-ChildItem -LiteralPath $app -Recurse -File).Count",
        "'installed: {0:N1} MB in {1} files ({2} bytes)' -f ($size / 1000000), $count, $size",
    )
    defender = install_script(
        "defender",
        "$status = Get-MpComputerStatus -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue",
        fail_unless("$status", "Defender's state could not be read: the proof needs its real-time protection on"),
        "\"Defender: real-time protection $($status.RealTimeProtectionEnabled), signatures of $($status.AntivirusSignatureLastUpdated)\"",
        fail_unless("$status.RealTimeProtectionEnabled", "Defender's real-time protection is off: the proof needs it on"),
        "$admin = ([Security.Principal.WindowsPrincipal][Security.Principal.WindowsIdentity]::GetCurrent()).IsInRole([Security.Principal.WindowsBuiltInRole]::Administrator)",
        "if (-not $admin) { 'the scan of the folder needs an administrator, and this account is none: not run (the first start under real-time protection, next, is the proof)'; exit 0 }",
        "$scanner = Join-Path $env:ProgramFiles 'Windows Defender\\MpCmdRun.exe'",
        "& $scanner -Scan -ScanType 3 -File $app 2>&1 | ForEach-Object { \"$_\" }",
        fail_unless(native_ok, "Defender's scan of the program folder found something or could not run", '"MpCmdRun ended with $LASTEXITCODE"'),
    )
    stop_entry = "$stop = Start-Process -FilePath (Join-Path $app 'neoaprsw.exe') -ArgumentList 'stop' -PassThru; $stop.WaitForExit()"
    daemon = install_script(
        "daemon", DATA_FOLDER, WAIT_PAGE, "$log = Join-Path $data 'neoaprs.log'",
        stop_entry,
        fail_unless("$stop.ExitCode -eq 0", "the Start menu's Stop NeoAPRS (neoaprsw.exe stop) failed with nothing running"),
        "$clock = [Diagnostics.Stopwatch]::StartNew()",
        "$p = Start-Process -FilePath (Join-Path $app 'neoaprsw.exe') -ArgumentList 'run' -PassThru",
        "$url = Wait-Page $log $p 180",
        fail_unless("$url", "neoaprsw.exe run served no page", "Get-Content -LiteralPath $log -Tail 30 -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue"),
        "$code = (Invoke-WebRequest $url -UseBasicParsing).StatusCode",
        "\"the page $url answered $code, $([int]$clock.Elapsed.TotalSeconds) s after the first start of the daemon\"",
        fail_unless("$code -eq 200", "the page does not answer"),
        "$request = [Net.HttpWebRequest]::Create($url + 'basemap-world.pmtiles'); $request.AddRange(0, 126)",
        "$answer = $request.GetResponse(); $head = New-Object byte[] 7; $null = $answer.GetResponseStream().Read($head, 0, 7); $status = [int]$answer.StatusCode; $answer.Close()",
        fail_unless("$status -eq 206 -and [Text.Encoding]::ASCII.GetString($head) -eq 'PMTiles'", "the world map that ships with the app is not served"),
        "'the world map is served'",
        "$description = (Get-Process -Id $p.Id).Description",
        "\"Task Manager: neoaprsw.exe, $description\"",
        fail_unless(f"$description -eq {ps_quote(DESCRIPTIONS['neoaprsw'])}", "neoaprsw.exe does not say what it is"),
        stop_entry,
        fail_unless("$p.WaitForExit(60000)", "the daemon did not end after Stop NeoAPRS"),
        fail_unless("(Get-Content -LiteralPath $log -Tail 1) -like '*NeoAPRS ended'", "the daemon did not end cleanly", "Get-Content -LiteralPath $log -Tail 10"),
    )
    support_out = ps_quote(ip.support)
    commands = install_script(
        "commands",
        "$exe = Join-Path $app 'neoaprs.exe'",
        *version_lines(version),
        "$doctor = & $exe doctor 2>&1 | ForEach-Object { \"$_\" } | Out-String",
        "$doctor",
        fail_unless("$doctor -notmatch 'Traceback' -and $doctor -match 'serial port'", "neoaprs.exe doctor did not run to its end (it lists the serial ports)"),
        f"& $exe support --out {support_out} 2>&1 | ForEach-Object {{ \"$_\" }}",
        fail_unless(native_ok, "neoaprs.exe support failed"),
        f"$zips = @(Get-ChildItem -LiteralPath {support_out} -Filter 'neoaprs-support-*.zip')",
        fail_unless("$zips.Count -eq 1", "the support logs made no file"),
        "Add-Type -AssemblyName System.IO.Compression.FileSystem",
        "$zip = [IO.Compression.ZipFile]::OpenRead($zips[0].FullName); try { $names = @($zip.Entries | ForEach-Object { $_.FullName }) } finally { $zip.Dispose() }",
        *(fail_unless(f"$names -contains {ps_quote(n)}", f"{n} is not in the support file") for n in ("README.txt", "summary.txt", "settings.json", "doctor.txt", "database.txt", "packets.txt", "logs/neoaprs.log")),
        "\"support file: $($zips[0].Name), $($names.Count) files\"",
    )
    app = install_script(
        "app", WAIT_PAGE,
        f"$data = {ps_quote(ip.data_app)}", "New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path $data | Out-Null", "$log = Join-Path $data 'neoaprs.log'",
        "$clock = [Diagnostics.Stopwatch]::StartNew()",
        "$p = Start-Process -FilePath (Join-Path $app 'neoaprs-app.exe') -ArgumentList '--tray', '--data', $data -PassThru",
        "$url = Wait-Page $log $p 180",
        fail_unless("$url", "the app did not start its daemon", "Get-Content -LiteralPath (Join-Path $data 'neoaprs-app.log'), $log -Tail 30 -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue"),
        "$code = (Invoke-WebRequest $url -UseBasicParsing).StatusCode",
        "\"the app's daemon: the page $url answered $code, $([int]$clock.Elapsed.TotalSeconds) s after the app's first start\"",
        fail_unless("$code -eq 200", "the page does not answer"),
        "Start-Sleep 5",                                    # (the tray icon is shown by pystray's own thread, whose failure is only a line of the app's log)
        fail_unless("-not $p.HasExited", "the app ended by itself", "Get-Content -LiteralPath (Join-Path $data 'neoaprs-app.log') -Tail 30"),
        "$applog = Join-Path $data 'neoaprs-app.log'",
        fail_unless("(Test-Path -LiteralPath $applog) -and -not (Select-String -LiteralPath $applog -Pattern 'uncaught exception|Traceback' -Quiet)", "the app logged an uncaught exception (its tray icon or its window failed)",
                    "Get-Content -LiteralPath $applog -Tail 40 -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue"),
        "$description = (Get-Process -Id $p.Id).Description",
        "\"Task Manager: neoaprs-app.exe, $description\"",
        fail_unless(f"$description -eq {ps_quote(DESCRIPTIONS['neoaprs-app'])}", "neoaprs-app.exe does not say what it is"),
        "& (Join-Path $app 'neoaprs.exe') stop --data $data 2>&1 | ForEach-Object { \"$_\" }",
        fail_unless(native_ok, "neoaprs.exe stop failed"),
        fail_unless("$p.WaitForExit(30000)", "the app did not end with its daemon", "Get-Content -LiteralPath (Join-Path $data 'neoaprs-app.log') -Tail 30"),
    )
    map_cut = install_script(
        "map",
        f"& (Join-Path $app 'neoaprs.exe') map --data {ps_quote(ip.data_map)} --lat 60.17 --lon 24.94 --radius 10 --maxzoom 8 --dry-run 2>&1 | ForEach-Object {{ \"$_\" }}",
        fail_unless(native_ok, "the map cut (a dry run) failed"),
    )
    sound_card = install_script(                            # (a type whose program the installation does not find is not offered, and `db radios add` refuses it with 2; the banner proves the program runs here, its DLLs with it)
        "direwolf",
        f"& (Join-Path $app 'neoaprs.exe') db --data {ps_quote(ip.data_direwolf)} radios add direwolf 2>&1 | ForEach-Object {{ \"$_\" }}",
        fail_unless(native_ok, "the installed app does not find its own Direwolf: the type Sound card is not offered"),
        "$said = (& (Join-Path $app 'bin\\direwolf\\direwolf.exe') -h 2>&1 | ForEach-Object { \"$_\" } | Out-String)",
        "$said",
        fail_unless(f"$said.Contains({ps_quote(direwolf)})", "the installed direwolf.exe does not run as the Direwolf NeoAPRS ships"),
    )
    python_env = [f"$env:Path = {ps_quote(paths.uv_dir + ';')} + $env:Path", *(f"$env:{name} = {ps_quote(value)}" for name, value in STEP_ENVIRONMENT.items() if name != "NEOAPRS_NO_DEVICES"),
                  f"Set-Location -LiteralPath {ps_quote(ip.kit)}"]
    smoke = install_script(
        "smoke", *python_env,
        f"& uv run --no-project --with {ps_quote('tornado==' + tornado)} scripts\\smoke.py --command (Join-Path $app 'neoaprs.exe') 2>&1 | ForEach-Object {{ \"$_\" }}",
        fail_unless(native_ok, "scripts/smoke.py failed against the installed neoaprs.exe"),
    )
    mercury = install_script(
        "mercury", *python_env,
        "& uv run --no-project packaging\\windows\\smoke_mercury.py (Join-Path $app 'bin\\mercury\\mercury.exe') 2>&1 | ForEach-Object { \"$_\" }",
        fail_unless(native_ok, "the installed Mercury does not listen on this computer alone"),
    )
    uninstall = uninstall_script(ip.uninstall_log)
    times = {"install": 600.0, "defender": 1800.0, "smoke": 900.0, "uninstall": 600.0}
    scripts = dict(zip(INSTALL_STEP_NAMES, (install, defender, daemon, commands, app, map_cut, sound_card, smoke, mercury, uninstall)))
    return [(name, scripts[name], times.get(name, 300.0)) for name in INSTALL_STEP_NAMES]


def kit_script(paths: Paths, ip: InstallPaths) -> str:
    tar = "$env:SystemRoot + '\\System32\\tar.exe'"
    return "\n".join(["$ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'", f"New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path {ps_quote(ip.kit)} | Out-Null",
                      f"& ({tar}) -xf {ps_quote(ip.kit_tar)} -C {ps_quote(ip.kit)}", "if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { exit $LASTEXITCODE }", f"Remove-Item -LiteralPath {ps_quote(ip.kit_tar)}", "exit 0"])


def put_python_kit(settings: Settings, paths: Paths, ip: InstallPaths, kit: Path, cache: Path) -> None:
    """uv and the kit on the machine, for the two steps that run Python: only now, so that every step before them ran where nothing but Windows and the app was."""
    put_uv_there(settings, paths, cache)
    copy_to(settings, kit, ip.kit_tar)
    remote_must(settings, kit_script(paths, ip), "the smoke scripts could not be unpacked on the machine")


def execute_install(settings: Settings, installer: Path, version: str, tornado: str, direwolf: str, kit: Path, cache: Path) -> int:
    """The install proof, from a machine that answers to the last result line. Nothing follows a failed install; every other step runs to its end, the uninstall last."""
    paths = windows_paths(settings.user, run_name(time.time()))
    ip = install_paths(paths, installer.name)
    log_dir = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="neoaprs-check-windows-install-"))
    say(f"the logs are in {log_dir}")
    make_root(settings, paths)
    remote_must(settings, f"$ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'; New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path {ps_quote(paths.run)} | Out-Null; exit 0", "the folder of the run could not be made")
    say(f"copying {installer.name} to {paths.run}")
    copy_to(settings, installer, ip.setup)
    results: list[StepResult] = []
    total = time.monotonic()
    python_ready: bool | None = None
    try:
        for name, script, timeout_sec in install_steps(paths, installer.name, version, tornado, direwolf):
            if results and results[0].code != 0:
                break
            if name in NEEDS_PYTHON:
                if python_ready is None:
                    try:
                        put_python_kit(settings, paths, ip, kit, cache)
                        python_ready = True
                    except Refused as error:
                        python_ready = False
                        log = log_dir / "python.log"
                        log.write_text(f"{error}\n", encoding="utf-8")
                        results.append(StepResult("python", 1, 0.0, log, (str(error),)))
                        print("\n".join(report_lines(results[-1])), flush=True)
                if not python_ready:
                    continue
            result = run_script(settings, paths, name, script, timeout_sec, log_dir)
            results.append(result)
            print("\n".join(report_lines(result)), flush=True)
    finally:
        remove_old_runs(settings, paths)
    print(summary(results, time.monotonic() - total), flush=True)
    return exit_code(results)


# ---- the upgrade proof (--upgrade) ----

# The one test, before a release is public, that a station of the release before comes through the update on Windows: the old installer on the clean machine, a station made with that release's own command line and
# run by its own daemon (its database at its own schema version, made-up stations heard), the new installer over it as an update is, then the new release on the same data folder: the radios made of the flat settings,
# the copy taken before the migration, the daemon twice (the second start migrates nothing), and the uninstall. Each step needs the one before: the first that fails ends the proof.
UPGRADE_STEP_NAMES = ("old", "station", "update", "migrate", "data", "daemon", "uninstall")
OLD_FILES = ("neoaprs.exe", "neoaprsw.exe", "neoaprs-app.exe", "unins000.exe")     # what every release before has in its program folder
# The station, by the flat keys of the release before (0.18.2: neoaprs/config.py SETTINGS; `neoaprs db set KEY VALUE`, neoaprs/cli/dbcmd.py), in an order that every step of it is a station that release takes:
# the Dummy radio as the FM radio (tncprofile.py DUMMY, "dummy") and the Dummy HF radio as the HF radio (DUMMY_HF, "dummy-hf"), so that no device and no sound card is needed.
STATION = (("station/call", "OH2GBA-9"), ("station/lat", "60.1699"), ("station/lon", "24.9384"), ("station/comment", "NeoAPRS upgrade proof"), ("beacon/interval_min", "30"), ("beacon/power_w", "5"),
           ("beacon/path", "WIDE1-1"), ("tnc/profile", "dummy"), ("hf/profile", "dummy-hf"), ("hf/enabled", "true"))
KEPT_KEYS = ("station/call", "station/lat", "station/lon", "station/comment", "beacon/interval_min", "beacon/power_w")     # the keys of the station that keep their names
# The flat keys that became a radio's (neoaprs/configradios.py FLAT_HOMES): the radio, and its column in `db radios` (type, on) or its own key there.
MOVED = {"tnc/profile": (1, "type"), "fm/enabled": (1, "on"), "beacon/path": (1, "radio/1/path"), "hf/profile": (2, "type"), "hf/enabled": (2, "on")}
RADIO_KINDS = {1: "fm", 2: "hf"}
RUN_SEC = 40                                                   # how long each daemon runs: the Dummy radios make a station heard every few seconds
APP_ID = "{5AE53960-2902-4F1B-99E1-03E486EA7B36}"             # packaging/windows/neoaprs.iss: AppId, the one Apps entry of every release
UNINSTALL_KEY = f"HKCU:\\Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Uninstall\\{APP_ID}_is1"
MIGRATED = "brought up to date now|is now version [0-9]+ [(]was [0-9]+[)]|a copy of it is in"     # the lines of neoaprs/migrations.py when a start migrates
LOG_TROUBLE = "Z  (ERROR|CRITICAL)  |Traceback"


class UpgradePaths(NamedTuple):
    old_setup: str
    new_setup: str
    old_log: str
    new_log: str
    uninstall_log: str
    data: str            # the station's data folder, the proof's own
    old_list: str        # what the old release's command line said of it
    old_stations: str


def upgrade_paths(paths: Paths, old_name: str, new_name: str) -> UpgradePaths:
    run = paths.run
    return UpgradePaths(f"{run}\\{old_name}", f"{run}\\{new_name}", f"{run}\\install-old.log", f"{run}\\install-new.log", f"{run}\\uninstall.log", f"{run}\\data-upgrade",
                        f"{run}\\old-db-list.txt", f"{run}\\old-db-stations.txt")


def version_key(version: str) -> tuple[int, ...]:
    return tuple(int(part) for part in version.split("-")[0].split("."))


def upgrade_versions(old: Path, new: Path) -> tuple[str, str]:
    """The versions of the two installers, the old one before the new one, or NotSetUp with the sentence."""
    old_version, new_version = installer_version(old, "--upgrade"), installer_version(new, "--upgrade")
    if old_version == new_version or version_key(old_version) > version_key(new_version):
        raise NotSetUp(f"--upgrade takes the installer of the release before, then the new one: {old.name} is not older than {new.name}")
    return old_version, new_version


def section(title: str, command: str, why: str, keep: str = "") -> list[str]:
    """A command of the installed neoaprs.exe under a line `### TITLE` (the proof reads its output by these titles), its output kept in the file `keep` too; a failure ends the step and says why."""
    lines = [f"'### {title}'", f"$out = @(& $exe {command} 2>&1 | ForEach-Object {{ \"$_\" }}); $code = $LASTEXITCODE", "$out"]
    if keep:
        lines.append(f"$out | Set-Content -LiteralPath {ps_quote(keep)} -Encoding UTF8")
    return [*lines, fail_unless("$code -eq 0", why, '"it ended with $code"')]


def daemon_lines(no_devices: bool) -> list[str]:
    """The installed daemon on the station's folder for RUN_SEC, with the update check off (and, for a release that has the switch, no device opened): its page must answer, then `neoaprs.exe stop` ends it
    cleanly. Its own lines of the log are in $new."""
    return [
        "$env:NEOAPRS_UPDATE_CHECK = '0'", *(["$env:NEOAPRS_NO_DEVICES = '1'"] if no_devices else []),
        "$log = Join-Path $data 'neoaprs.log'",
        "$skip = if (Test-Path -LiteralPath $log) { @(Get-Content -LiteralPath $log).Count } else { 0 }",
        "$clock = [Diagnostics.Stopwatch]::StartNew()",
        "$p = Start-Process -FilePath (Join-Path $app 'neoaprsw.exe') -ArgumentList 'run', '--data', $data, '--web-port', '0' -PassThru",
        # (the page's address from the lines this start wrote: the log holds the runs before, each with its own)
        "$url = $null; foreach ($i in 1..180) { $m = Get-Content -LiteralPath $log -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | Select-Object -Skip $skip | Select-String 'web page at (http://\\S+/)' | Select-Object -Last 1; "
        "if ($m) { $url = $m.Matches[0].Groups[1].Value; break }; if ($p.HasExited) { break }; Start-Sleep 1 }",
        fail_unless("$url", "neoaprsw.exe run served no page", "Get-Content -LiteralPath $log -Tail 30 -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue"),
        "$code = (Invoke-WebRequest $url -UseBasicParsing).StatusCode",
        "\"the page $url answered $code, $([int]$clock.Elapsed.TotalSeconds) s after the start\"",
        fail_unless("$code -eq 200", "the page does not answer"),
        f"$wait = {RUN_SEC} - [int]$clock.Elapsed.TotalSeconds; if ($wait -gt 0) {{ Start-Sleep $wait }}",
        fail_unless("-not $p.HasExited", "the daemon ended by itself", "Get-Content -LiteralPath $log -Tail 30"),
        "& $exe stop --data $data 2>&1 | ForEach-Object { \"$_\" }",
        fail_unless(NATIVE_OK, "neoaprs.exe stop failed"),
        fail_unless("$p.WaitForExit(60000)", "the daemon did not end after neoaprs.exe stop"),
        fail_unless("(Get-Content -LiteralPath $log -Tail 1) -like '*NeoAPRS ended'", "the daemon did not end cleanly", "Get-Content -LiteralPath $log -Tail 10"),
        "$new = @(Get-Content -LiteralPath $log | Select-Object -Skip $skip)",
        "\"the daemon ran $([int]$clock.Elapsed.TotalSeconds) s and wrote $($new.Count) lines to its log\"",
    ]


HEARD_LINES = ["'### heard'", "$new | ForEach-Object { if ($_ -match '  INFO  ([A-Z0-9]+(-[0-9]+)?)>') { $Matches[1] } } | Sort-Object -Unique"]     # the calls of the packets the daemon logged


def clean_log_lines() -> list[str]:
    return ["$trouble = @($new | Where-Object { $_ -match " + ps_quote(LOG_TROUBLE) + " })",
            fail_unless("$trouble.Count -eq 0", "the daemon's log has an ERROR or a Traceback since this start", "$trouble | Select-Object -First 30")]


def upgrade_steps(paths: Paths, old_name: str, old_version: str, new_name: str, new_version: str) -> list[tuple[str, tuple[str, ...], float]]:
    """The steps of the upgrade proof in order, each its name, its scripts (one after the other on the machine: a command line holds only so much) and its time. Every command of `old` and `station` is one the
    release before takes (the module's docstring names the source)."""
    up = upgrade_paths(paths, old_name, new_name)
    station_folder = [f"$data = {ps_quote(up.data)}", "$exe = Join-Path $app 'neoaprs.exe'"]
    old = install_script("old", *setup_lines(up.old_setup, up.old_log), *files_lines(OLD_FILES), *version_lines(old_version))
    pairs = ", ".join(f"@({ps_quote(key)}, {ps_quote(value)})" for key, value in STATION)
    sets = [f"$pairs = @({pairs})",
            "foreach ($kv in $pairs) { & $exe db --data $data set $kv[0] $kv[1] 2>&1 | ForEach-Object { \"$_\" }; if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { \"the old release's command line refused $($kv[0]) $($kv[1])\"; exit 1 } }"]
    station = (install_script("station", *station_folder, *sets, *daemon_lines(no_devices=False)),
               install_script("station", *station_folder,
                              *section("old db list", "db --data $data list", "the old release's db list failed", up.old_list),
                              *section("old db stations", "db --data $data stations", "the old release's db stations failed", up.old_stations)))
    update = install_script(
        "update", *setup_lines(up.new_setup, up.new_log), *files_lines(INSTALLED_FILES), *version_lines(new_version),
        fail_unless("-not (Test-Path -LiteralPath (Join-Path $app 'bin\\pmtiles.exe'))", "the update left bin\\pmtiles.exe of an earlier release"),
        f"$entry = Get-ItemProperty -LiteralPath {ps_quote(UNINSTALL_KEY)} -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue",
        "\"the Apps list: $($entry.DisplayName) $($entry.DisplayVersion)\"",
        fail_unless(f"$entry.DisplayVersion -eq {ps_quote(new_version)}", f"the Apps list does not say NeoAPRS {new_version}"),
    )
    migrate = install_script(
        "migrate", *station_folder, *daemon_lines(no_devices=True), *clean_log_lines(),
        f"$moved = @($new | Where-Object {{ $_ -match {ps_quote(MIGRATED)} }})", "$moved",
        fail_unless("@($moved | Where-Object { $_ -match 'brought up to date now' }).Count -eq 1", "the first start of the new release did not migrate the database"),
        fail_unless("@($moved | Where-Object { $_ -match 'a copy of it is in .*premigrate-v[0-9]+' }).Count -eq 1", "the migration took no copy of the database before it"),
    )
    data = install_script(
        "data", *station_folder,
        *section("db radios", "db --data $data radios", "neoaprs.exe db radios failed on the updated station"),
        *section("db list", "db --data $data list", "neoaprs.exe db list failed on the updated station"),
        *section("db restore", "db --data $data restore", "neoaprs.exe db restore (the list of the copies) failed"),
        *section("db stations", "db --data $data stations", "neoaprs.exe db stations failed on the updated station"),
        *section("doctor", "doctor --data $data", "neoaprs.exe doctor found something to fix on the updated station"),
    )
    daemon = install_script(
        "daemon", *station_folder, *daemon_lines(no_devices=True), *clean_log_lines(), *HEARD_LINES,
        f"$moved = @($new | Where-Object {{ $_ -match {ps_quote(MIGRATED)} }})",
        fail_unless("$moved.Count -eq 0", "the second start of the new release migrated again", "$moved"),
        "'the second start migrated nothing'",
    )
    times = {"old": 600.0, "update": 600.0, "uninstall": 600.0}
    scripts = dict(zip(UPGRADE_STEP_NAMES, (old, station, update, migrate, data, daemon, uninstall_script(up.uninstall_log))))
    return [(name, script if isinstance(script, tuple) else (script,), times.get(name, 300.0)) for name, script in scripts.items()]


def sections(text: str) -> dict[str, list[str]]:
    """A step's output cut at its lines `### TITLE`: the lines under each title."""
    found: dict[str, list[str]] = {}
    lines: list[str] | None = None
    for line in text.splitlines():
        if line.startswith("### "):
            lines = found.setdefault(line[4:].strip(), [])
        elif lines is not None:
            lines.append(line.rstrip())
    return found


LISTED = re.compile(r"(\S+) +(.*?) {2,}(\S.*)$")         # a line of `db list`: the key, the value, and whether it is stored (columns two spaces apart; the value has none)
RADIO = re.compile(r"radio (\d+)  (.+?)  (\S+)  (\S+)  (on|off|removed .+?)  \(position \d+\)$")      # a radio of `db radios`: number, name, kind, type, state
STATION_ROW = re.compile(r"(\S+) +\S+ +\d{4}-\d\d-\d\d \d\d:\d\d:\d\dZ ")          # a row of `db stations`: the call first
# The copy of the database the first start of the new release takes, named by the schema version of the release before: 26 for 0.18.2 (v0.18.2:neoaprs/migrations.py, MIGRATIONS is _v1 to _v26 and
# SCHEMA_VERSION = len(MIGRATIONS)). Any number is taken, and said: the proof is of the update, whichever release is the one before.
COPY = re.compile(r"premigrate-v(\d+)\S*")


def listing(lines: Sequence[str]) -> dict[str, str]:
    """The keys of `db list` (or of a radio in `db radios`) and their values as they are shown."""
    found = {}
    for line in lines:
        matched = LISTED.match(line.strip())
        if matched and "/" in matched.group(1):
            found[matched.group(1)] = matched.group(2)
    return found


@dataclass(frozen=True)
class Radio:
    kind: str
    type: str
    state: str
    settings: dict[str, str]


def radios(lines: Sequence[str]) -> dict[int, Radio]:
    found: dict[int, Radio] = {}
    current: Radio | None = None
    for line in lines:
        matched = RADIO.match(line)
        if matched:
            current = found[int(matched.group(1))] = Radio(matched.group(3), matched.group(4), matched.group(5), {})
        elif current is not None and line.startswith("  "):
            current.settings.update(listing([line]))
    return found


def station_calls(lines: Sequence[str]) -> list[str]:
    return [matched.group(1) for line in lines if (matched := STATION_ROW.match(line)) and matched.group(1) != "call"]


Checked = tuple[list[str], list[str]]        # what is wrong, and what is said when nothing is


def check_station(outputs: Mapping[str, str]) -> Checked:
    """The station as the old release keeps it: every value it was given, and stations its daemon heard."""
    old = sections(outputs.get("station", ""))
    kept = listing(old.get("old db list", []))
    problems = [f"the old release's db list has {key} as {kept.get(key)!r}, not {value!r}" for key, value in STATION if kept.get(key) != value]
    call = dict(STATION)["station/call"]
    heard = [c for c in station_calls(old.get("old db stations", [])) if c != call]
    if not heard:
        problems.append("the old release's daemon heard no station of its Dummy radios (db stations lists none)")
    return problems, [f"the station of the release before: {len(kept)} rows in its db list, {len(heard)} stations heard besides its own"] if not problems else []


def check_data(outputs: Mapping[str, str]) -> Checked:
    """The updated station against what the old release kept: the settings that keep their names, the radios made of the flat keys, exactly one copy from before the migration, the stations, the doctor."""
    old, new = sections(outputs.get("station", "")), sections(outputs.get("data", ""))
    was, now = listing(old.get("old db list", [])), listing(new.get("db list", []))
    problems = [f"{key} was {was.get(key)!r} and is {now.get(key)!r} after the update" for key in KEPT_KEYS if now.get(key) != was.get(key)]
    found = radios(new.get("db radios", []))
    for number, kind in RADIO_KINDS.items():
        keys = [key for key, (radio, _) in MOVED.items() if radio == number]
        wanted = number == 1 or was.get("hf/enabled") == "true"
        radio = found.get(number)
        if radio is None or radio.kind != kind:
            if wanted:
                problems.append(f"db radios has no radio {number}, the {kind.upper()} radio that {' and '.join(keys)} made")
            continue
        for key in keys:
            column = MOVED[key][1]
            shown = radio.type if column == "type" else ("true" if radio.state == "on" else "false") if column == "on" else radio.settings.get(column)
            if shown != was.get(key):
                problems.append(f"radio {number} has {column} {shown!r}, and the old {key} was {was.get(key)!r}")
    copies = [line for line in new.get("db restore", []) if COPY.match(line)]
    notes = []
    if not copies:
        problems.append("db restore lists no copy premigrate-v...: the migration left no copy of the database from before it")
    elif len(copies) > 1:
        problems.append(f"db restore lists {len(copies)} copies premigrate-v...: one is kept, the latest ({'; '.join(copy.split()[0] for copy in copies)})")
    elif "taken before the update" not in copies[0]:
        problems.append(f"db restore does not mark {copies[0].split()[0]} as taken before the update")
    else:
        name = copies[0].split()[0]
        notes.append(f"the copy taken before the update: {name} (schema version {name.removeprefix('premigrate-v').split('-')[0]} of the release before)")
    problems += [f"doctor: {line.strip()}" for line in new.get("doctor", []) if line.startswith("FAIL")]
    calls = set(station_calls(new.get("db stations", [])))
    lost = [c for c in station_calls(old.get("old db stations", [])) if c not in calls]
    if lost:
        problems.append(f"db stations has lost {len(lost)} of the stations the old release knew: {' '.join(lost[:10])}")
    return problems, notes if not problems else []


def check_daemon(outputs: Mapping[str, str]) -> Checked:
    """The new daemon heard again stations that the old one heard: the Dummy radios came through the update."""
    call = dict(STATION)["station/call"]
    before = {c for c in station_calls(sections(outputs.get("station", "")).get("old db stations", [])) if c != call}
    heard = {line.strip() for line in sections(outputs.get("daemon", "")).get("heard", []) if line.strip()}
    again = sorted(before & heard)
    if not again:
        return ["the new daemon heard none of the stations the old one heard: the Dummy radios did not come through the update"], []
    return [], [f"heard again after the update: {' '.join(again[:8])}{' ...' if len(again) > 8 else ''}"]


UPGRADE_CHECKS: dict[str, Callable[[Mapping[str, str]], Checked]] = {"station": check_station, "data": check_data, "daemon": check_daemon}


def checked(result: StepResult, outputs: Mapping[str, str]) -> StepResult:
    """A step that passed on the machine, held to what the proof reads from its output (and from the steps before): a problem fails it, with the problems under its line and at the end of its log."""
    check = UPGRADE_CHECKS.get(result.name)
    if result.code != 0 or check is None:
        return result
    problems, notes = check(outputs)
    for note in notes:
        say(note)
    if not problems:
        return result
    with result.log.open("a", encoding="utf-8") as log:
        log.write("".join(f"{problem}\n" for problem in problems))
    return StepResult(result.name, 1, result.seconds, result.log, tuple(problems))


def run_parts(settings: Settings, paths: Paths, name: str, parts: Sequence[str], timeout_sec: float, log_dir: Path) -> StepResult:
    """A step of more than one script: each run as run_script runs one, until one fails, and their output one log under the step's name."""
    if len(parts) == 1:
        return run_script(settings, paths, name, parts[0], timeout_sec, log_dir)
    results: list[StepResult] = []
    for index, part in enumerate(parts, 1):
        results.append(run_script(settings, paths, f"{name}-{index}", part, timeout_sec, log_dir))
        if results[-1].code != 0:
            break
    log = log_dir / f"{name}.log"
    log.write_text("".join(result.log.read_text(encoding="utf-8", errors="replace") for result in results), encoding="utf-8")
    for result in results:
        result.log.unlink()
    last = results[-1]
    return StepResult(name, last.code, sum(result.seconds for result in results), log, last.tail)


def execute_upgrade(settings: Settings, old: Path, old_version: str, new: Path, new_version: str) -> int:
    """The upgrade proof, from a machine that answers to the last result line. Each step needs the ones before it: none follows a failed step."""
    paths = windows_paths(settings.user, run_name(time.time()))
    up = upgrade_paths(paths, old.name, new.name)
    log_dir = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="neoaprs-check-windows-upgrade-"))
    say(f"the logs are in {log_dir}")
    make_root(settings, paths)
    remote_must(settings, f"$ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'; New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path {ps_quote(paths.run)} | Out-Null; exit 0", "the folder of the run could not be made")
    for installer, target in ((old, up.old_setup), (new, up.new_setup)):
        say(f"copying {installer.name} to {paths.run}")
        copy_to(settings, installer, target)
    results: list[StepResult] = []
    outputs: dict[str, str] = {}
    total = time.monotonic()
    try:
        for name, parts, timeout_sec in upgrade_steps(paths, old.name, old_version, new.name, new_version):
            result = run_parts(settings, paths, name, parts, timeout_sec, log_dir)
            outputs[name] = result.log.read_text(encoding="utf-8", errors="replace")
            result = checked(result, outputs)
            results.append(result)
            print("\n".join(report_lines(result)), flush=True)
            if result.code != 0:
                break
    finally:
        remove_old_runs(settings, paths)
    print(summary(results, time.monotonic() - total), flush=True)
    return exit_code(results)


# ---- the command ----

def interrupted(number: int, frame: FrameType | None) -> None:
    raise KeyboardInterrupt


def parse(argv: Sequence[str], split: Callable[[Sequence[str]], tuple[list[str], list[str]]]) -> tuple[argparse.Namespace, list[str]]:
    own, pytest_args = split(argv)
    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog="check-windows", usage="scripts/check-windows [--only NAME]... [--snapshot NAME] [--tty] [-- PYTEST-ARGS...]\n       scripts/check-windows --install INSTALLER --snapshot NAME\n       scripts/check-windows --upgrade OLD-INSTALLER NEW-INSTALLER --snapshot NAME",
                                     description=__doc__, formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter)
    parser.add_argument("--only", action="append", default=[], choices=[step.name for step in steps(windows_paths("x", "x"))], metavar="NAME", help="run only this step (repeatable): sync lock ruff pytest smoke")
    parser.add_argument("--snapshot", default="", metavar="NAME", help="put the machine back to this snapshot before it is started (only while it is powered off)")
    parser.add_argument("--tty", action="store_true", help="run the pytest step through ssh -tt without trying a plain session first")
    parser.add_argument("--install", default="", metavar="INSTALLER", help="the install proof of this NeoAPRS-Setup-VERSION.exe, on the machine put back to --snapshot, instead of the CI's steps")
    parser.add_argument("--upgrade", nargs=2, default=[], metavar=("OLD", "NEW"), help="the upgrade proof: the installer of the release before, a station made with it, then this NeoAPRS-Setup-VERSION.exe over it, "
                        "on the machine put back to --snapshot, instead of the CI's steps")
    args = parser.parse_args(own)
    if args.install and args.upgrade:
        parser.error("--install and --upgrade are two proofs: one at a time")
    for option, given in (("--install", args.install), ("--upgrade", args.upgrade)):
        if not given:
            continue
        if args.only or pytest_args or args.tty:
            parser.error(f"{option} runs its proof alone: no --only, --tty or arguments for pytest with it")
        if not args.snapshot:
            parser.error(f"{option} starts from a clean machine: give --snapshot NAME, the snapshot of the clean Windows")
    if pytest_args and args.only and "pytest" not in args.only:
        parser.error("arguments after -- are for pytest, and --only does not name it")
    if pytest_args and not args.only:
        args.only = ["pytest"]
    return args, pytest_args


def main(argv: Sequence[str] | None = None) -> int:
    packer = load_script("check-in-container")
    args, pytest_args = parse(sys.argv[1:] if argv is None else argv, packer.split_command)
    try:
        settings = read_settings(os.environ)
        for tool in ("ssh", "scp", "VBoxManage", "git"):
            if shutil.which(tool) is None:
                raise NotSetUp(f"{tool} is not installed (the Windows check needs ssh, scp, VBoxManage and git)")
        problems = missing_files(settings)
        if problems:
            raise NotSetUp("; ".join(problems))
        installer = Path(args.install)
        version = installer_version(installer) if args.install else ""
        tornado = tornado_pin((ROOT / "pyproject.toml").read_text(encoding="utf-8")) if args.install else ""
        direwolf = direwolf_banner((ROOT / "neoaprs" / "direwolf.py").read_text(encoding="utf-8")) if args.install else ""
        old, new = (Path(args.upgrade[0]), Path(args.upgrade[1])) if args.upgrade else (Path(), Path())
        old_version, new_version = upgrade_versions(old, new) if args.upgrade else ("", "")
    except NotSetUp as error:
        say(str(error))
        return NOT_SET_UP
    cache = build_cache(os.environ)
    # The tree (or, for the install proof, the smoke scripts; for the upgrade proof nothing) is packed into a file before the machine is asked for anything: what is wrong with it is said while nothing runs yet.
    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix="neoaprs-check-windows-tar-") as scratch:
        tar = Path(scratch) / "tree.tar"
        try:
            if args.install:
                pack_kit(ROOT, tar)
            elif not args.upgrade:                              # (the upgrade proof takes nothing of the tree: the two installers are all)
                with tar.open("wb") as out:
                    packer.pack(ROOT, out)
        except (packer.NotPacked, OSError) as error:
            say(f"nothing was run: {error}")
            return NOT_SET_UP
        for number in (signal.SIGINT, signal.SIGTERM, signal.SIGHUP):
            signal.signal(number, interrupted)
        started_by_us = False
        try:
            with run_lock(lock_path(os.environ, settings.vm)):
                plan = plan_power(vm_state(settings.vm), args.snapshot, settings.vm)
                if plan.start:
                    started_by_us = True
                    start_vm(settings, plan, args.snapshot)
                wait_for_ssh(settings, SSH_PATIENCE_SEC if plan.start else 60.0)
                if plan.start:
                    wait_until_settled(settings)
                if args.upgrade:
                    return execute_upgrade(settings, old, old_version, new, new_version)
                if args.install:
                    return execute_install(settings, installer, version, tornado, direwolf, tar, cache)
                return execute(settings, chosen_steps(args.only), pytest_args, tar, cache, args.tty)
        except (Refused, Busy) as error:
            say(str(error))
            return NOT_SET_UP
        except KeyboardInterrupt:
            say("interrupted")
            return 130
        finally:
            if started_by_us:
                signal.signal(signal.SIGINT, signal.SIG_IGN)       # (the shutdown is not given up on by a second Ctrl+C)
                power_off(settings)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
